	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/first_person/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How wide you see from a vehicle's third-person seats (driver, gunner), in degrees across a 16:9 screen. Passenger seats use your Field of View. Default keeps the game's view; Match uses your Field of View. Above 150 needs Panini Projection.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 20 to 160."/>
		<string text="How far a scope zooms at your Field of View. Xbox zooms to the same view whatever yours is, as the Xbox did. Scaled zooms your own view by the same magnification, so a wider view stays wider zoomed."/>
		<string text="Stops a wide field of view from stretching what is at the sides; you still see as far, and the middle is drawn larger. 1 keeps their shapes true. The HUD stays flat. Fields of view up to 160 need it.|Click the number (or press A) to type 0 to 1."/>
		<string text="With Panini Projection on: straightens floors and ceilings above and below the middle, and stretches the sides taller. 0 keeps their shapes true.|Click the number (or press A) to type 0 to 1."/>
		<string text="How far the world is drawn (the far clip), in world units of about 3 meters. Default is the game's 1024, which the stock maps fit in; farther shows more of a large custom map.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 1024 to 10000."/>
		<string text="Puts the reticle below the middle of the screen, as Halo 2 and 3 do. Your view tilts up a little, so shots still go where the reticle points. Zooming centers it."/>
		<string text="How far below the middle the lowered reticle sits, in percent of the screen's height. 10 is about Halo 2's and 3's.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 0 to 30."/>
		<string text="Riding in a Warthog or a Scorpion in the campaign and co-op: the view from behind the vehicle, or from your seat. Behind, the weapon cannot zoom."/>
		<string text="Your weapon and hands: whether they are drawn, their field of view and their place. Your legs, and your shield's flare on your arms, its color and an overshield's."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
